  "review_conclusions": [
    "Public compatibility assessment first uses semver VersionReq.matches. Directional analysis is only for a failed positive match and requires proof over the full admitted interval; ambiguous prerelease,empty,unrepresentable and overflow cases stay conservative. This is not complete project or engine admission.",
    "EngineVersion and requirement constructors centralize parse validation. Serializable assessment snapshots are observations rather than renewed trust or file admission; derivations are not dynamic registration or FFI.",
    "Summary byte and string entry points apply raw input length before migration, then bound tree complexity and root counts using different units. The public value loader itself requires an already bounded caller; CR-PROJECT-0003 remains an open intent question, not a newly confirmed BUG.",
    "MigrationChain validates and applies schema steps before typed decoding. v1-to-v2 introduces historical defaults; v2-to-v3 upgrades the version while identity/admission obligations remain in summary/full-manifest validation.",
    "SummaryDocument deliberately projects a subset of the full manifest: unknown extra fields are ignored,wrong types of represented fields fail,and current-version project identity requirements differ from migrated legacy inputs. Direct serde construction of a result does not repeat byte,filesystem or compatibility admission.",
    "Runtime's full-manifest loader reuses migration parsing but explicitly rejects migrated input and performs its own validation. Editor preflight/template callers consume the shared summary for bounded observations and later decisions.",
    "All21 tests and all mounted scopes were read; fixture paths resolve from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR to repository-root tests/fixtures/serialization/project-manifest. These contexts receive no formal R027 coverage."
  ],
